 of being able to  be a speaker and be on stage and get  paid to do what you're doing you got to  start at the beginning  so you start small you start doing you  know small events it could be at the  library or local charities or local  events and you know you might not get  paid at the beginning to do it you just  practicing your craft  what that will do is is help hone your  message and also make you more  comfortable out there speaking in front  of people and getting used to the types  of questions that will come at you and  they'll make your presentation better  and better and better and better and  better when I first started doing public  speaking it wasn't with a goal to be a  public speaker it was more just to help  entrepreneurs so it sold my business and  I stopped you know I want to give back  and want to help other entrepreneurs and  I created a series to help entrepreneurs  learn from the lessons that I had gone  through and I just did it you know  through my local YMCA at the beginning  and I think the first first time I did  had three or four people in it so really  tiny and then it you know we just  continue doing it and continue growing  in the built up momentum behind that and  eventually partnered up with a bank and  hosted it their event and then group you  know too big for that so we partnered up  with our bookstores and whole you know  held huge events we had lots of people  coming out to the seminars and it was a  lot of fun for me be able to give back  you offer value to entrepreneurs and it  also made me better you know my first  presentations the content was good but  how I delivered it wasn't great you know  he got it gets better every time you  practice just like doing these videos I  get better and better every time we do  the videos if you go back and watch the  first videos the content was still  pretty good but maybe the delivery  wasn't fantastic so as you do more and  more you get better so people start to  recognize you people start to give you  referrals people start to say oh you  should be speaking up here or I want you  to come speak up my company or whatever  it is so you have to be able to practice  practice practice and eventually you'll  get better and people will recognize you  the other thing I would do is try to  become a media expert so whatever your  message is there are going to be stores  written about it in the media and the  media are always looking for experts to  comment on whatever that story is and  why shouldn't you be that expert so you  want to make a list of reporters who  follow your industry or who write about  interesting stories for you and whenever  they do write an article comment on it  give them feedback and let them know who  you are and give you a perspective it's  not just being promotional and saying  you know I'm Molly and here's what I do  you want to give them something extra  you want to show that you are really an  expert so that they're gonna want to  contact you if they have another story I  also use a service called PR leads which  is 100 bucks a month where reporters  will give you stories so they'll tell  you the service are working on and  they're looking for experts so you can  just email them and say no here's a I'm  an expert and here's why and you give  them feedback on it on their story that  they're working on so I find that  helpful so start speaking try to be a  media expert the last thing I would do  is if you're trying to get a public  speaking gig try working on your YouTube  videos as well I don't know if you've  done YouTube at all but it's a great way  to get your message out and if you're a  speaker you should try to speak as much  as you can now you know when you're  doing a YouTube video you're speaking to  the camera instead of speaking to an  audience we just kind of have to pretend  that there's a huge audience in front of  you and not just you in a room speaking  but it's a great way to get your message  out for you to also practice your crap  and for people to see how good you are  so most of my speaking now is from you  two questions just like this one the  question you ask but I'll also do others  from you know profiles of successful  entrepreneurs in lessons you can learn  for you you might not have people asking  you questions yet but you can just go to  forums that are related to your topic  and see what people are writing about  and say that you're gonna create a video  reply and when you you know create your  video say I'm creating this video in  response to whoever who asks a question  about XYZ that relates to your topic so  I try to get consistent on you know  creating these videos building up a  following getting people to see you and  it makes you better homes your message  even more and you'll get gigs so you  know from what I was doing just just  from those public speaking things that  I'd set up here in my city I then got  invited eventually to go speak at  various events around the world or  flying to - as far away as Brunei Taiwan  to speak at different events and it  comes from starting at that you know  small scale - beginning now I never had  that vision - wanna go on be a speaker  just kind of happened but for you if you  have a clear plan  you know you got to practice as much as  you can get as many games as you can  free just to get your message home and  to get people to know you and continue  building on that don't try to be a media  expert and try to create some YouTube  videos again to practice your craft and  be seen as the expert and you're on your  way to be able to be a speaker to  hopefully get paid and have a really  fulfilling career so while I hope that  helps for those watching if you guys  have something else to add please leave  a comment below I'd love to hear how  you've gotten some speaking gigs or if  you have another question or any  suggestions from Molly please leave a  comment and if you liked the video  please give it a thumbs up I love making  these videos to help you guys out and  always appreciate those thumbs ups  coming in makes me know that you guys  like the videos and keep making more so  thank you for your support and we'll see  you on the next episode  you
 

